coder › Implemented `wrap(text, width)` in `src/wrap.ts` and added tests in `src/wrap.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/wrap.ts`
  - Throws `RangeError` when `width < 1`.
  - Splits input into paragraphs on blank (whitespace-only) lines, normalizing `\r\n`/`\r` first.
  - Within a paragraph, collapses runs of whitespace into one space and trims.
  - Wraps greedily, breaking at spaces so no line exceeds `width`, and splits any word longer than `width` into full-width chunks.
  - Joins paragraphs with exactly one blank line (`\n\n`), so multiple blank lines collapse to one and the output has no trailing spaces on any line.

Decisions not spelled out in the request
- Single line breaks inside a paragraph (no blank line between them) are treated as spaces, since only blank lines separate paragraphs.
- Whitespace-only lines count as blank paragraph separators.
- `\r\n` and `\r` line endings are normalized to `\n`.

